          </li>
          <li>
            <strong>Constitutional Vacation Bonus (Terço Constitucional):</strong> In Brazil, employees are legally entitled to 30 days of paid vacation plus an additional one-third (33.3%) of their monthly salary as a holiday bonus. This adds an effective 2.78% to total annual payroll.
          </li>
          <li>
            <strong>FGTS Severance Indemnity Reserve:</strong> Brazilian employers remit 8% of monthly earnings into the employee’s government severance fund (FGTS). If terminated without statutory cause, the employer must pay an additional 40% penalty on the total accumulated FGTS balance.
          </li>
        </ul>
        <p>
          By contrast, in Poland and Romania, while statutory vacation is generous (20 to 26 business days), there is no mandatory 13th-month salary requirement in the private tech sector. The gross contract salary divided by 12 equals the actual monthly base.
        </p>
